---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="About | Colorado Elopement Guide" description="Who runs Colorado Elopement Guide, how listings work, and how the site makes money.">
  <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-5 md:px-8 pt-14">
    <h1 class="display text-4xl leading-tight">About this <span class="serif-i">guide</span></h1>
    <div class="mt-6 space-y-5 text-ink/75 leading-relaxed">
      <p>Colorado Elopement Guide is an independent directory of Colorado's elopement and micro-wedding vendors, run by Ryan Bynum. It exists because finding vendors who genuinely work small weddings — a sunrise ceremony at Sapphire Point, ten guests at a Lyons barn — shouldn't require digging through platforms built for 200-person ballrooms.</p>
      <p><strong>How listings work:</strong> we compile every listing from public business information and Google Business Profile data (with AI assistance, reviewed before publishing), and every listing is free, permanently. Vendors can claim their listing to correct details, add photos and packages, and receive monthly reports of the real clicks and inquiries their page generated — bot-filtered, never inflated.</p>
      <p><strong>How we make money:</strong> one way only — vendors can pay $40/month for Featured placement, which is always labeled. Placement never changes the Google ratings shown, we never write or alter reviews, and no vendor can pay to make a competitor disappear.</p>
      <p><strong>Something wrong?</strong> If you're listed and want changes — or want out — <a href="/claim" class="underline underline-offset-4">claim your listing</a> or <a href="/contact" class="underline underline-offset-4">contact us</a>; removals happen within one business day.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
